--- THG2-04: a whole instance of a member-declaring type prints ---
a milestone called i1.
Set i1's 'the bearing in degrees' to 027.
Print i1.

--- THG2-19: copy, print, compare, mutate, compare again on a member-declaring type ---
a milestone called i2.
Set i2's 'the bearing in degrees' to 027.
a milestone called i3 is i2.
Print i3.
If i2 is not i3 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-19: expected i2 to equal i3", Exit 95. Print i2.
Set i3's 'the bearing in degrees' to 378.
If i2 is i3 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-19: expected i2 to differ from i3", Exit 95. Print i2.

--- THG2-29: free call and instance possessive agree on the same ordinary function ---
a cairn called i4.
Set i4's 'the chain length' to -000027.
a number called c1 is 'the balance so far' of i4.
a number called c2 is i4's 'the balance so far'.
If c1 is not c2 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-29: expected {c2} got {c1}", Exit 95. Print c1.

--- THG2-34: the type possessive maker call, field read back ---
a milestone called i5 is a milestone's 'planted deep' with 027.
If i5's 'the margin' is not 27 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-34: expected 27 got {i5's 'the margin'}", Exit 95. Print i5's 'the margin'.

--- THG2-38: a receiver reached by both the instance and type possessive agree ---
a milestone called i6.
a milestone called i7 is i6's 'inverted through'.
a milestone called i8 is a milestone's 'inverted through' on i6.
If i7 is not i8 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-38: expected i7 to equal i8", Exit 95. Print i7.

--- THG2-44: two different types sharing a field name do not collide ---
A thing called 'the fix' has
    a number called drift is -00027.

A thing called 'the boundary stone' has
    a number called drift is -00931.

a 'the fix' called i9.
a 'the boundary stone' called i10.
Set i9's drift to -077651.
Set i10's drift to 0006.
If i9's drift is not -77651 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected -77651 got {i9's drift}", Exit 95. Print i9's drift.
If i10's drift is not 6 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected 6 got {i10's drift}", Exit 95. Print i10's drift.

--- a program with no things at all: the manifest-dependent leaves stand aside ---
Print 0 minus 0.

Print 0 times 0.

Print 0 times 0.

Print 0 add 0.

Print 0 minus 0.

--- THG2-44 stays available even with zero things (it never reads the manifest) ---
A thing called 'the station' has
    a number called 'the bearing in degrees'.

A thing called 'the anchorage' has
    a number called 'the bearing in degrees' is -0273511210.

a 'the station' called i11.
a 'the anchorage' called i12.
Set i11's 'the bearing in degrees' to 09469.
Set i12's 'the bearing in degrees' to 8.
If i11's 'the bearing in degrees' is not 9469 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected 9469 got {i11's 'the bearing in degrees'}", Exit 95. Print i11's 'the bearing in degrees'.
If i12's 'the bearing in degrees' is not 8 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected 8 got {i12's 'the bearing in degrees'}", Exit 95. Print i12's 'the bearing in degrees'.

--- nested forms (indent, nested=true) ---
  a milestone called i13,
  Set i13's 'the bearing in degrees' to 027,
  Print i13.

  a milestone called i14,
  Set i14's 'the run' to 931,
  a milestone called i15 is i14,
  Print i15,
  If i14 is not i15 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-19: expected i14 to equal i15", Exit 95. Print i14,
  Set i15's 'the run' to -077651,
  If i14 is i15 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-19: expected i14 to differ from i15", Exit 95. Print i14.

  a cairn called i16,
  Set i16's 'the chain length' to 0006,
  a number called c3 is 'the balance so far' of i16,
  a number called c4 is i16's 'the balance so far',
  If c3 is not c4 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-29: expected {c4} got {c3}", Exit 95. Print c3.

  a milestone called i17 is a milestone's 'planted deep' with 9,
  If i17's 'the margin' is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-34: expected 9 got {i17's 'the margin'}", Exit 95. Print i17's 'the margin'.

  a milestone called i18,
  a milestone called i19 is i18's 'inverted through',
  a milestone called i20 is a milestone's 'inverted through' to i18,
  If i19 is not i20 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-38: expected i19 to equal i20", Exit 95. Print i19.

A thing called 'the fix' has
    a number called drift.

A thing called 'the boundary stone' has
    a number called drift.

  a 'the fix' called i21,
  a 'the boundary stone' called i22,
  Set i21's drift to 0000077,
  Set i22's drift to -0000504453,
  If i21's drift is not 77 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected 77 got {i21's drift}", Exit 95. Print i21's drift,
  If i22's drift is not -504453 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-44: expected -504453 got {i22's drift}", Exit 95. Print i22's drift.

